    <string name="a11y_disclosure_title">Accessibility service</string>
    <string name="a11y_disclosure_message">To block apps, PureLock needs Android\'s Accessibility service.\n\nWhat it does: it sees which app comes to the front, and while a lock is active it checks whether a Settings screen is showing PureLock, to send you home.\n\nWhat it does not do: it does not read what you type or your messages, and nothing it sees is stored or sent anywhere.\n\nYou can turn it off any time in Android settings.</string>
    <string name="a11y_agree_open">I understand, open settings</string>
    <string name="a11y_continue_without">Start without app blocking</string>
    <string name="a11y_after_enable">Turn on PureLock under Accessibility, then start the lock again.</string>
    <string name="owner_title">Device Owner (optional)</string>
    <string name="owner_message">Device Owner gives stronger protection: while a lock is active, uninstalling and force-stopping PureLock is blocked.\n\nIt can only be set up by you, on a device with no accounts added (or after a factory reset), from a computer with USB debugging:\n\n%s\n\nPureLock never turns this on by itself. Emergency calls always keep working.</string>
